use ../../../lib/UiComponent

from ../../buttons/Button import Button

export ui-component Timer:
    description:
        A timer shows time running, either counting down to zero, like an oven
        timer, or counting up from zero, like a stopwatch. It can be started,
        paused, resumed and reset.

    composes:
        - @{Button}

    countdown:
        Counting down starts from a length of time the component gives, such
        as 5 minutes, and stops at zero.

    stopwatch:
        Counting up starts from zero, or from a time the component gives. It
        keeps going until stopped, or the component can give a time to stop at.

    controls:
        Buttons start, pause, resume and reset it, and restart it from the
        beginning. Only the ones that make sense are available, so a running
        timer can be paused but not started. The component can do all of these
        itself, and can start the timer as soon as it appears.

    display:
        It shows the time in parts, such as hours, minutes and seconds, with
        leading zeros, like `05:09`. The component chooses which parts to show,
        and whether to include days or fractions of a second. How often the
        display changes is up to the component, once a second by default.

    accuracy:
        The time shown is worked out from the clock, not by counting updates,
        so it stays right even if the page is busy or hidden for a while.

    finishing:
        When it reaches zero, or the time to stop at, it stops and the
        component is told. The component is also told each time it changes, if
        it wants to be.

    assistiveTools:
        It is marked as a timer and has a name, such as "Time left".
        Assistive tools can read out the current time whenever they look, but
        aren't told about every change, which would be noise. When the timer
        finishes, the component can tell them using Announcement.

    nonGoals:
        - Not a clock showing the time of day
        - No laps, alarms, or sounds. The app can add those
        - It doesn't carry on after the page is reloaded. An app that needs
            that keeps the start time itself
